#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# --- node ---
node_modules/

# --- nested repos, archived out of this tree 2026-09-11 ---
# Kept as rules so a stray re-clone here does not get committed by accident.
#
# `portfolio/` WAS on this list and had to come off it on 2026-10-16. It named
# an abandoned Next.js attempt archived in 2026-09-11 -- and then the site
# directory was renamed `3d_portfolio` -> `portfolio` and collided with it.
# Nothing appeared to break: git does not untrack files already tracked, so
# the rename committed cleanly and the build passed. Only NEW files under the
# site were silently dropped, which is how nine freshly split constants
# modules reached main as a barrel importing nothing. CI caught it.
test/
innit/
SathishKumarAI/
sathishkumarai.github.io/

# Portrait source. The optimised 600x750 crop in 3d_portfolio/public/ is what
# ships; this 1MB original stays local.
/HeadShot.jpg

# Saved LinkedIn profile page (45MB, ~58 files incl. tracking scripts and
# recaptcha). Kept locally as a content source; never committed.
Satish Kumar _ LinkedIn.html
Satish Kumar _ LinkedIn_files/

# A screenshot dropped at the root in September and never referenced by
# anything. Ignored rather than deleted: it is not the repo's to throw away,
# and an untracked file that shows up in every `git status` eventually gets
# committed by accident.
/download.png

# Impeccable critique snapshots: local design-review artefacts, not site source
.impeccable/
